## height
# THE OPEN HILLSIDE.  Every cell is authored ('0' is ordinary ground): an unauthored cell is
# procedural and the smoothing pass would bridge the one cliff this map is made of.  The pasture is
# a single gently rolling field, 0 to 6 voxels, with no step anywhere above one voxel — the whole
# map is walkable and it is all one region.  The old raised block at x26-30 / x35-41 is gone; it was
# an accident of the flat tile map, and it was what made the map's 188-voxel jump-only region.
#
# THE LENS SHELF (LOOT.md {{LOOT_PASTURE}}), the map's ONE jump-only region, against the fold's
# west wall.  All of it is terrain, not stamps, because a stamp's top is solid:
#   x23-26 z19-24   the ramp up out of the grass, one voxel a cell, so walking gets you onto
#   x23-26 z16-18   the bank along the fold wall, at 6 — walk-reachable, region 1
#   x23-26 z14-15   TWO empty cells at ground level.  Leaving the bank at z=15.76 and landing at
#                   z<=13.24 is 2.48 cells; a running jump carries 3.6 and a standing one 2.2, so
#                   the run clears it and the walk does not.  Three cells would be 3.48, inside 4%
#                   of the limit — that is why it is two.
#   x23-26 z12-13   THE SHELF at 7, one voxel above the bank, which is inside the two a jump gains.
#                   Every other neighbour of the shelf is the apron at 0, seven voxels down, so
#                   walking can never reach it and the drop off is free.  The find is `nightsight`:
#                   without the herder there is nothing on that hillside to see.
# The apron x21-28 z10-26 is held flat at 0 so the rolling ground cannot erode any of those numbers.
